course: dictionary
lesson: 148
title: Affiliate: joined to a bigger group
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Affiliate can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, to affiliate means to join or connect officially with a larger group or organisation. As a noun, an affiliate is the smaller group, company or person that is officially connected to a bigger one. «The local station is an affiliate of a national network.» The small station is officially connected to the big network.
explain: Look for the clue words around it. You will often see «affiliated with» or «affiliated to», as in «a club is affiliated to a league». Clubs, schools, TV channels and companies can all be affiliated. The word «affiliated» tells you there is a link, and the bigger group is usually named after it.
explain: Read the money sentence: «An affiliate is paid for each sale they bring; a £20 product with 10% off costs £18, and the YouTuber might get £2 for the sale.» Here the affiliate is the YouTuber, a person officially linked to the seller. They are paid for each sale they bring in, so the word must mean someone connected to a bigger business.
fact: Affiliate is a verb and a noun. As a verb it means to join or connect officially with a larger group.
fact: As a noun, an affiliate is a smaller group, company or person officially connected to a bigger one.
fact: «Affiliated with» and «affiliated to» both mean officially connected to a group, such as a club and its league.
fact: «An affiliate of» a network means a smaller station or company that is officially linked to that network.
fact: A good check is to swap in the words «officially connected to» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «An affiliate is paid for each sale they bring.» Who is the affiliate in this sentence? | *A person officially connected to the seller | A customer who buys a product | A bank that keeps the money | A product that costs £20
exercise: «The club is affiliated to a national league.» What does affiliated mean here? | *Officially joined to the league | Shouting at the referee | Chased out of the league | Playing in a different country
exercise: «The local station is an affiliate of a national network.» Find and copy the word that means a smaller group officially linked to a bigger one. | network | *affiliate | station | national
test: «The school is affiliated with a larger sports association.» What does affiliated mean? | Bigger than the association | *Officially connected to the association | Sold to the association | Banned from the association
test: Which of these is an affiliate? | *A TV station officially linked to a national network | A sunny beach | A bread roll | A rainy afternoon
exam: In «An affiliate is paid for each sale they bring», who gets paid? | The customer who buys | The company that makes the product | *The affiliate, who is officially linked to the seller | The bank that holds the money
